# AgileSpace Project Patterns

## Architecture Overview

AgileSpace follows a clean architecture with strict separation of concerns:

- **Components**: Pure UI rendering in [src/components/](mdc:src/components/)
- **Hooks**: Business logic in [src/hooks/](mdc:src/hooks/)
- **API Layer**: Supabase queries/mutations in [src/lib/supabase/](mdc:src/lib/supabase/)
- **Types**: TypeScript definitions in [src/types/](mdc:src/types/)

## Required Patterns

### ✅ Component Structure

```tsx
// src/components/feature-name.tsx
import { useFeatureName } from "@/hooks/use-feature-name";

export function FeatureName({ prop }: FeatureNameProps) {
  const { data, loading, handleAction } = useFeatureName({ prop });

  if (loading) return <LoadingSpinner />;

  return <div className="feature-container">{/* UI only */}</div>;
}
```

### ✅ Hook Structure

```tsx
// src/hooks/use-feature-name.ts
export function useFeatureName({ prop }: UseFeatureNameProps) {
  // All logic here
  return { data, loading, actions };
}
```

### ✅ API Layer

- Queries in [src/lib/supabase/queries.ts](mdc:src/lib/supabase/queries.ts)
- Mutations in [src/lib/supabase/mutations.ts](mdc:src/lib/supabase/mutations.ts)
- Use TanStack Query for data fetching

### ✅ Required Imports

```tsx
// UI Components
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge";

// Utils
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// Types
import type { Tag, Session } from "@/types";
```

## AgileSpace-Specific Rules

### Hierarchical Tags Implementation

- Use [useHierarchicalTagSelector](mdc:src/hooks/use-hierarchical-tag-selector.ts) for tag logic
- Categories and subcategories from [issue-types.ts](mdc:src/constants/issue-types.ts)
- Seed predefined types with `seedIssueTypes` function

### Session Management

- All session logic in custom hooks
- Use TanStack Query for session data
- Handle optimistic updates for better UX

### Styling Conventions

- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Follow [AgileSpace design system](mdc:src/components/ui/)
- Ensure accessibility with proper ARIA attributes

### Error Handling

- Use error boundaries for component errors
- Handle API errors in hooks with TanStack Query
- Provide user-friendly error messages

## File Organization

```
src/
├── components/           # Pure UI components
│   ├── ui/              # Design system components
│   └── feature-name.tsx # Feature-specific components
├── hooks/               # Business logic hooks
│   ├── api/            # API-related hooks
│   └── use-*.ts        # Feature hooks
├── lib/
│   ├── supabase/       # Database layer
│   └── utils.ts        # Utility functions
├── types/              # TypeScript definitions
└── constants/          # Application constants
```

## Quality Standards

- **TypeScript**: Strict typing, no `any`
- **Performance**: Use React.memo, useCallback, useMemo appropriately
- **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
- **Testing**: Separate logic from UI for better testability
